# Rank 1050 / CVE-2022-24440: cocoapods-downloader passed a Podfile-supplied git
# URL to git as a positional argument, so a value beginning with `--` became an
# option (CWE-74, CWE-88). Git.preprocess_options in
# lib/cocoapods-downloader/git.rb built
#
#   command = ['ls-remote', options[:git], options[:branch]]
#   output = Git.execute_command('git', command)
#
# and `:git => '--upload-pack=touch ./HELLO1;'` runs that command. The fix
# 52a0d54464 rejects any value starting with `--` or containing ` --`, and adds
# `--` to the command as an argument separator.
#
# ATTENTION. The vocabulary for this weakness is right and the plumbing is
# missing, in three separable places.
#
#  - The sink concept is orphaned. code.CommandOptionInjectionSink exists with
#    cwe CWE_74 and CWE_88 and vulnerableTo injection.ArgumentInjection, four
#    bindings emit it, and no rule in vyql/packs consumes it. Only the presence
#    issue code.CommandOptionInjection has a rule, VYQL-INJ-031, so argument
#    injection cannot be reported by taint anywhere, in any language.
#  - Ruby command execution through backticks is invisible. execute_command in
#    api.rb runs `\n#{executable} #{command} 2>&1`, and neither that form nor a
#    plain `#{cmd}` is labelled a sink; a probe binding on callee.method == "`"
#    matches nothing, so the frontend does not present a backtick as a call at
#    all. The 18 Ruby command bindings cover system, exec, spawn, the Kernel
#    forms, IO.popen and Open3, which is every way of running a command except
#    the most idiomatic one.
#  - No control describes the fix. There is no concept for an argument separator
#    or for rejecting a leading dash, and String#shellescape is unbound, only
#    Shellwords.escape and Shellwords.shelljoin are, so the escaping this file
#    does is unlabelled too.
#
# One thing is already correct and should not be changed while fixing the rest:
# core.ProcessArgVector neutralizes injection.CommandInjection only, so the array
# form at git.rb:26, which vyql match does label, will not wrongly suppress an
# argument-injection finding once one can be raised.
#
# Scanning lib/ reports 6 findings at the vulnerable revision, 3 VYQL-PATH-001,
# 2 VYQL-RF-001 and 1 VYQL-RES-001, all in remote_file.rb and none in git.rb.
# The sources are present: vyql match labels eight code.ExternalEntryInput rows
# in git.rb through library.param-source, including the one this CVE starts from.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-orphaned-sink

test "rank1050: a caller-supplied git URL becomes a git option"
  lang ruby
  file lib/cocoapods-downloader/git.rb
  profile library
  reject VYQL-INJ-031
  code
  ```
  module Pod
    module Downloader
      class Git < Base
        def self.preprocess_options(options)
          return options unless options[:branch]

          command = ['ls-remote',
                     options[:git],
                     options[:branch]]
          output = Git.execute_command('git', command)
          match = commit_from_ls_remote output, options[:branch]

          return options if match.nil?

          options[:commit] = match
          options.delete(:branch)

          options
        end

        def self.execute_command(executable, command, raise_on_failure = false)
          require 'shellwords'
          command = command.map(&:to_s).map(&:shellescape).join(' ')
          output = `\n#{executable} #{command} 2>&1`
          output
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1050: fix rejects a leading dash and separates the arguments"
  lang ruby
  file lib/cocoapods-downloader/git.rb
  profile library
  reject VYQL-INJ-031
  code
  ```
  module Pod
    module Downloader
      class Git < Base
        def self.preprocess_options(options)
          return options unless options[:branch]

          input = [options[:git], options[:commit]].map(&:to_s)
          invalid = input.compact.any? { |value| value.start_with?('--') || value.include?(' --') }
          raise DownloaderError, "Provided unsafe input for git #{options}." if invalid

          command = ['ls-remote',
                     '--',
                     options[:git],
                     options[:branch]]

          output = Git.execute_command('git', command)
          match = commit_from_ls_remote output, options[:branch]

          return options if match.nil?

          options[:commit] = match
          options.delete(:branch)

          options
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1050: neither backtick form is labelled a command sink"
  lang ruby
  file lib/cocoapods-downloader/api.rb
  profile library
  reject VYQL-INJ-031
  code
  ```
  module Pod
    module Downloader
      module API
        def run(executable, command)
          out1 = `#{executable} #{command}`
          out2 = `\n#{executable} #{command} 2>&1`
          [out1, out2]
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```
